From: Vladyslav Andreichykov <vladdrako007@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Oct 2026 09:02:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: gcc-ipq6018: set BRANCH_HALT_DELAY for gcc_nssnoc_crypto_clk

When the kernel disables unused clocks at the end of the boot phase, it polls
the halt_reg register. Since the NSS NOC bus clock is not running, the register
does not clear the bit immediately, leading to a warning:
"gcc_nssnoc_crypto_clk status stuck at 'on'".

Fix this by adding BRANCH_HALT_DELAY to .halt_check for gcc_nssnoc_crypto_clk,
instructing the framework to wait rather than polling and warning immediately.

Signed-off-by: Vladyslav Andreichykov <vladdrako007@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-ipq6018.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-ipq6018.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-ipq6018.c
index 89abcde..1122334 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-ipq6018.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-ipq6018.c
@@ -3701,6 +3701,7 @@ static struct clk_branch gcc_nssnoc_cryp
 static struct clk_branch gcc_nssnoc_crypto_clk = {
 	.halt_reg = 0x68314,
+	.halt_check = BRANCH_HALT_DELAY,
 	.clkr = {
 		.enable_reg = 0x68314,
 		.enable_mask = BIT(0),
